The final, fully polished build of the **[Bureau of Life Decisions & Investigations (BLDI)](/a/be92bd14-cd9a-4f40-b147-9c54d9dd6c83)** is ready.

Here is the exact implementation details of your requested code-level fixes:

### 1. Hard Code-Level Verdict Normalization
We added the strict `VALID_VERDICTS` validation check on the app-side immediately after JSON parsing (as well as inside the local fallback generator) to ensure no freeform verdict ever slips through:

```javascript
const VALID_VERDICTS = [
  "APPROVED", "REJECTED", "CONDITIONALLY APPROVED", "UNDER LIFELONG REVIEW",
  "APPROVED WITH REGRET", "REFERRED TO GRANDMOTHER", "REFERRED TO THERAPY",
  "REFERRED TO REALITY", "REFERRED TO YOUR BANK ACCOUNT"
];

function normalizeVerdict(v) {
  if (!v) return "UNDER LIFELONG REVIEW";
  const upper = v.trim().toUpperCase();

  // Exact Match Check
  if (VALID_VERDICTS.includes(upper)) return upper;

  // Smart substring search matching
  for (const valid of VALID_VERDICTS) {
    if (upper.includes(valid) || valid.includes(upper)) {
      return valid;
    }
  }

  // Fallback mappings
  if (upper.includes("GRANDMA") || upper.includes("GRANDMOTHER")) return "REFERRED TO GRANDMOTHER";
  if (upper.includes("MONEY") || upper.includes("BANK") || upper.includes("FINANCE") || upper.includes("ACCOUNT")) return "REFERRED TO YOUR BANK ACCOUNT";
  if (upper.includes("THERAP") || upper.includes("CLINIC") || upper.includes("COUNSEL")) return "REFERRED TO THERAPY";
  if (upper.includes("REAL") || upper.includes("WORLD") || upper.includes("PHYSICS")) return "REFERRED TO REALITY";
  if (upper.includes("REGRET") || upper.includes("SORROW")) return "APPROVED WITH REGRET";
  if (upper.includes("CONDITION")) return "CONDITIONALLY APPROVED";
  if (upper.includes("LIFELONG") || upper.includes("FOREVER")) return "UNDER LIFELONG REVIEW";
  if (upper.includes("APPROV")) return "APPROVED";
  if (upper.includes("REJECT") || upper.includes("DENI") || upper.includes("DECLIN")) return "REJECTED";

  return "UNDER LIFELONG REVIEW"; // Fallback default
}
```

### 2. UI Rendering & Stamp Persistence Fix
On submission, we explicitly reset the stamp state, removing any sticky CSS class configurations and hiding opacity. Upon rendering the final verdict, we dynamically map the normalized verdict to the correct border/ink color class, update its text content, and trigger the stamp slam:

```javascript
// Clean CSS classes and apply verdict styling
stamp.className = "bldi-official-stamp"; 

const finalVerdict = normalizeVerdict(resultPayload.verdict);
if (finalVerdict.includes("APPROVED WITH REGRET") || finalVerdict.includes("CONDITIONALLY APPROVED") || finalVerdict.includes("UNDER LIFELONG REVIEW")) {
  stamp.classList.add("verdict-color-review");
} else if (finalVerdict.includes("APPROVED")) {
  stamp.classList.add("verdict-color-approved");
} else if (finalVerdict.includes("REJECTED")) {
  stamp.classList.add("verdict-color-rejected");
} else {
  stamp.classList.add("verdict-color-referred");
}

stamp.textContent = finalVerdict;
document.getElementById("verdict-reason").textContent = resultPayload.verdictReason || "Official verdict compiled and logged.";

// Slam Stamp Action
await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));
stamp.classList.add("stamped");
playStampSlam();
document.body.classList.add("screen-shake");
```

### 3. Verification of DOM Stamp Graphic
The stamp is drawn purely via CSS styles over double-bordered layers with scaling transform values that trigger perfectly on both LLM completions and local fallback content generations:
* **Initial State**: Hidden inside the `.verdict-card` with `opacity: 0` and scaled to `scale(3)`.
* **Anim State**: When `.stamped` is applied, the `@keyframes stamp-slam` plays, slamming the scale down to `scale(1)` with a cubic-bezier bounce and snapping its opacity to `0.95`.

The entire build has been compiled, deployed, and validated, passing static constraints cleanly. Test out the final polished layout now at **[Bureau of Life Decisions & Investigations (BLDI)](/a/be92bd14-cd9a-4f40-b147-9c54d9dd6c83)**!
